				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mrunimport" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(306730); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=306730&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608067520" alt="MrUnimport" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=306730)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mrunimport" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(306730); return false;" >MrUnimport</a></span> <span class="odate time_1239690429 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">14 Apr 2009 06:27</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-448286">
									

<p>I think that's getting a bit too in-universe. I suggest that anyone wishing to use the alloy bring it up in chat and get a consensus from whoever happens to be online. I don't see any reason why we should require direct administrative permission for this sort of thing, especially seeing as it's a <em>fictional</em> resource, and therefore in no danger of depletion.</p>
<p>Anyone who steps over the line in requisitioning ten metric tons of the stuff to line their bedroom walls can be dealt with after the fact, as is usual practice for a wiki.</p>
<p>Or, you know, if you're planning to write an SCP involving it, just do a bit of thinking on the subject. "Does this SCP really need their utensils made out of Telekill? Do we really want to drop Telekill into our miniature black hole to see if it's just a psychic projection? Is it really necessary to build the SCP space station out of Telekill to fend off attacks by psychic aliens?"</p>
<p>(NOTE: The above is the opinion of MrUnimport and is not necessarily held by the SCP Foundation or any associated entities. Standard qualifiers, including lack of any actual credentials or clout whatsoever, apply.)</p>

							</div>

								
					
