														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1496816">
									

<p>There are certain old things that don't get brought up much any more; PRI (Psionic Resistance Index) or some such being one of them. Telekill overtook them, but fell out of fashion for the same reason 682 references did: overuse. Suddenly everything was psychic that needed the magic metal to fix. even things that WEREN'T psychic were being shielded by 148 alloy because&#8230; Science?</p>
<p>Since the overarching canon and refined standards have been put up, cross-SCP usage is being thoroughly discouraged, and the use of 148 as such is pretty much verboten. About the only time you'll see it used is during a tale when the &quot;Oh Shit Button&quot; has already been pressed.</p>
<p>Beyond that, within a limited range of stuff it's up to the authors of individual things to come up with ways around psychic effects.</p>

