			<div class="content" id="post-content-1277026">
									

<p>I have an alternate idea:</p>
<p>We've agreed that Telekill is a cop-out. We've agreed that Telekill has been used way too much (though I figure a lot of the articles that used them have since been deleted). Yet some to most of us think it's useful at least <em>some</em> of the time.</p>
<p>Why don't we just say that it's all been used? It still works forever, there just isn't any more of it. If some gets freed up, we can say it was automatically allocated to something else as per standing orders. If a really, REALLY good SCP comes around that uses it, we can say some was freed up as above and allocated here. Then we decom or ARC it and say it can't be used again. We can throw something into either the site rules or the How To Write guide mandating it can only be de-decommissioned in very, very isolated conditions with Clef's permission (or three senior staff votes, or something) and any other use is grounds for automatic deletion (grandfathering in all the already-accepted uses).</p>
<p>This doesn't preclude a rewrite, just takes care of the loose end.</p>

