			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1278751">
									

<p>How about this: instead of telekill blocking psychic energy, it <em>scrambles</em> psychic energy which passes through it. And while that prevents the psychic energy from having it's intended effect, scrambled psychic energy is <em>bad</em>. If you wear a helmet make of telekill and a psychic tries to telepathically say &quot;Hello&quot; to you, the scrambled energy drives you insane. Line a room with telekill to contain a reality-warper whose powers are psychic in nature, he tries to use his powers to melt a hole through the telekill, and the scrambled energy rips a hole in the fabric of reality which lets all of 682's relatives come through.</p>
<p>This still leaves some uses for telekill:</p>
<ol>
<li>Line a room with it to prevent remote viewing.</li>
<li>Wear a helmet of it to prevent anyone from reading your mind.</li>
<li>Wear a helmet in circumstances where being driven insane is preferable to being mind-controlled.</li>
<li>A quick way to test if an SCP has any psychic component: put a helmet on a D-class and see if he goes insane.</li>
<li>Bullets which can punch through any shield a psychic might use.</li>
</ol>

